   {
    "text": "Once upon a time, in a cozy little town called Chillington, there lived a curious little boy named Timmy. Timmy was known for his love of riddles and his knack for finding the most absurd answers. One sunny afternoon, he stumbled upon a peculiar old man named Mr. Whiskers, who had a peculiar habit of sitting on a bench in the town square, staring at the sky with a thoughtful expression.\n\nMr. Whiskers had a peculiar way of speaking, always using words like \"mysterious\" and \"enigmatic,\" and he was known to say, \"I’ve got a riddle for you, young Timmy.\" Timmy, ever eager to play, said, \"What can you catch but not throw?\"\n\nMr. Whiskers chuckled and said, \"Ah, a classic! The answer is a *cold*.\"\n\nTimmy blinked, confused. \"But how can you catch a cold? You can’t just *catch* it like a fish!\"\n\nMr. Whiskers smiled and said, \"Exactly! You can *catch* a cold, but you can’t *throw* it. It’s like a *cold*—you can’t just throw it away, it just *comes* to you.\"\n\nTimmy was intrigued. \"So, what’s the trick here?\"\n\nMr. Whiskers leaned in and said, \"The trick is that a *cold* is something you can *catch* but not *throw*—it’s like a *cold* that just *comes* to you, and you can’t *throw* it away. It’s like a *cold* that just *comes* to you, and you can’t *throw* it away.\"\n\nTimmy grinned and said, \"So, I guess I should be careful not to catch a cold, but I can’t throw it either!\"\n\nMr. Whiskers nodded and said, \"Exactly! And remember, *catching* a cold is like *catching* a *cold*—it’s not something you can *throw* away. It’s something you can *catch* and then *feel*.\"\n\n*Timmy was now more careful about his health, and he made sure to keep his blanket warm in the winter.*  \n*He also made sure to keep his hat on when he went outside, just in case.*\n\nand that, my friends, is why you never try to toss a sneeze!",
